    answerJsonLd: "<p>You can edit a PDF for free with zero subscriptions, watermarks, or credit card requirements using RealEditPDF. Unlike traditional cloud services that restrict free users to 1–2 documents per day or lock text modification behind premium plans, RealEditPDF processes everything 100% client-side via WebAssembly. This allows you to edit text, redact private data, sign forms, and rearrange pages at full original quality without paying a penny.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-how-to-edit-pdf-on-mac",
    question: "how to edit a pdf on mac",
    category: "devices",
    categoryLabel: "macOS",
    shortKeywords: "how to edit a pdf on mac free safari chrome preview alternative adobe acrobat",
    answerHtml: `<p>To edit a PDF on Mac for free without buying Adobe Acrobat, open Safari or Google Chrome and navigate to <a href="https://realeditpdf.com/" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF.com</a>. While macOS includes the built-in Preview app, Preview cannot overwrite existing text or apply permanent data redactions. With RealEditPDF, simply drag your PDF from Finder into the browser window to insert text, cover and update paragraphs, draw legal signatures, stamp custom watermarks, and reorder pages. All processing runs locally in your Mac browser's memory for maximum speed and privacy.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>To edit a PDF on Mac for free without buying Adobe Acrobat, open Safari or Google Chrome and navigate to RealEditPDF.com. While macOS includes the built-in Preview app, Preview cannot overwrite existing text or apply permanent data redactions. With RealEditPDF, simply drag your PDF from Finder into the browser window to insert text, cover and update paragraphs, draw legal signatures, stamp custom watermarks, and reorder pages. All processing runs locally in your Mac browser's memory for maximum speed and privacy.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-what-is-a-100-free-pdf-editor",
    question: "What is a 100% free PDF editor?",
    category: "free",
    categoryLabel: "Free Editing",
    shortKeywords: "what is a 100% free pdf editor realeditpdf zero limits open source client side",
    answerHtml: `<p>A 100% free PDF editor is a tool that provides unrestricted document editing capabilities without hidden charges, subscriptions, task limits, or branded watermarks. <a href="#editor-anchor" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF</a> is 100% free forever because it is architected with client-side WebAssembly (WASM). By utilizing your computer or phone's local processing power rather than costly cloud servers, RealEditPDF provides unlimited text editing, digital signing, document redaction, and page management completely free of charge.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>A 100% free PDF editor is a tool that provides unrestricted document editing capabilities without hidden charges, subscriptions, task limits, or branded watermarks. RealEditPDF is 100% free forever because it is architected with client-side WebAssembly (WASM). By utilizing your computer or phone's local processing power rather than costly cloud servers, RealEditPDF provides unlimited text editing, digital signing, document redaction, and page management completely free of charge.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-can-i-edit-my-own-pdf",
    question: "Can I edit my own PDF?",
    category: "howto",
    categoryLabel: "How-To Guide",
