    answerHtml: `<p>Yes, you can easily edit your own PDF documents. Whether it is an employment resume, a business contract, a rental lease, or a tax form, simply drag your file into <a href="#editor-anchor" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF</a>. You can add new text, mask outdated information using the whiteout tool, insert checkboxes, place your signature, and organize pages. Because your files remain entirely in your local browser sandbox, your personal information is never uploaded to remote servers.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>Yes, you can easily edit your own PDF documents. Whether it is an employment resume, a business contract, a rental lease, or a tax form, simply drag your file into RealEditPDF. You can add new text, mask outdated information using the whiteout tool, insert checkboxes, place your signature, and organize pages. Because your files remain entirely in your local browser sandbox, your personal information is never uploaded to remote servers.</p>"
