    categoryLabel: "Mobile",
    shortKeywords: "can i edit a pdf on my phone iphone android ipad mobile browser",
    answerHtml: `<p>Yes, you can edit PDFs directly on your smartphone (iPhone, iPad, or Android) without downloading extra apps from the App Store or Google Play. Open your mobile browser (such as Safari or Chrome) and go to <a href="https://realeditpdf.com/" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF.com</a>. Tap <strong>Select PDF Document</strong> to choose a file from your device or cloud storage (Files app, iCloud, Google Drive). You can pinch to zoom, add typography, draw signatures with your touchscreen, and download the finished PDF in seconds.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>Yes, you can edit PDFs directly on your smartphone (iPhone, iPad, or Android) without downloading extra apps from the App Store or Google Play. Open your mobile browser (such as Safari or Chrome) and go to RealEditPDF.com. Tap Select PDF Document to choose a file from your device or cloud storage (Files app, iCloud, Google Drive). You can pinch to zoom, add typography, draw signatures with your touchscreen, and download the finished PDF in seconds.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-how-do-i-open-a-pdf-file",
    question: "How do I open a PDF file?",
    category: "basics",
    categoryLabel: "PDF Basics",
    shortKeywords: "how do i open a pdf file browser reader view edit acrobat alternative",
    answerHtml: `<p>You can open a PDF file on any computer or mobile device by double-clicking it to view in standard web browsers like Chrome, Safari, Edge, or Firefox. If you want to view and edit a PDF at the same time without installing standalone reader software, visit <a href="#editor-anchor" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF</a> and select your file. It renders instantaneously in your browser canvas ready for immediate text edits, signing, and page management.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>You can open a PDF file on any computer or mobile device by double-clicking it to view in standard web browsers like Chrome, Safari, Edge, or Firefox. If you want to view and edit a PDF at the same time without installing standalone reader software, visit RealEditPDF and select your file. It renders instantaneously in your browser canvas ready for immediate text edits, signing, and page management.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-what-is-a-pdf-file-used-for",
    question: "What is a PDF file used for?",
    category: "basics",
    categoryLabel: "PDF Basics",
    shortKeywords: "what is a pdf file used for portable document format contracts invoices printing",
    answerHtml: `<p>A PDF (Portable Document Format) is a universal document format designed by Adobe and standardized by ISO to present documents consistently across all software, hardware, and operating systems. PDF files are primarily used for contracts, employment agreements, business invoices, tax forms, eBooks, and printable brochures because they preserve exact typography, graphics, page numbering, and layouts on every device.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>A PDF (Portable Document Format) is a universal document format designed by Adobe and standardized by ISO to present documents consistently across all software, hardware, and operating systems. PDF files are primarily used for contracts, employment agreements, business invoices, tax forms, eBooks, and printable brochures because they preserve exact typography, graphics, page numbering, and layouts on every device.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-which-pdf-is-free-to-edit",
    question: "Which PDF is free to edit?",
    category: "free",
    categoryLabel: "Free Editing",
    shortKeywords: "which pdf is free to edit word google docs scans invoices non password protected",
    answerHtml: `<p>Any standard, unencrypted PDF document is free to edit using <a href="#editor-anchor" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF</a>. Whether your PDF was generated from Microsoft Word, exported from Google Docs, scanned from a physical document, or received via email, you can edit it for free. As long as the file does not have a restrictive owner password, you can modify text, annotate, e-sign, redact, and rearrange pages at no charge.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>Any standard, unencrypted PDF document is free to edit using RealEditPDF. Whether your PDF was generated from Microsoft Word, exported from Google Docs, scanned from a physical document, or received via email, you can edit it for free. As long as the file does not have a restrictive owner password, you can modify text, annotate, e-sign, redact, and rearrange pages at no charge.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-can-i-edit-a-pdf-without-paying",
    question: "Can I edit a PDF without paying?",
    category: "free",
    categoryLabel: "Free Editing",
    shortKeywords: "can i edit a pdf without paying free no credit card no trial no subscription",
    answerHtml: `<p>Yes, you can edit a PDF completely without paying. While enterprise tools like Adobe Acrobat Pro cost $13 to $20 per month, <a href="#editor-anchor" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF</a> offers all essential document editing features—including text insertion, smart whiteout replacement, e-signatures, permanent redactions, and page reorganization—100% free of charge with no trial period, no paywalls, and no credit card required.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>Yes, you can edit a PDF completely without paying. While enterprise tools like Adobe Acrobat Pro cost $13 to $20 per month, RealEditPDF offers all essential document editing features—including text insertion, smart whiteout replacement, e-signatures, permanent redactions, and page reorganization—100% free of charge with no trial period, no paywalls, and no credit card required.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-can-i-edit-a-pdf-without-adobe",
    question: "Can I edit a PDF without Adobe?",
    category: "howto",
    categoryLabel: "Alternative",
    shortKeywords: "can i edit a pdf without adobe acrobat creative cloud web alternative",
    answerHtml: `<p>Yes, you do not need Adobe Acrobat or an Adobe Creative Cloud subscription to edit PDF files. Web-based editors like <a href="#editor-anchor" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF</a> provide a complete set of editing tools directly inside your web browser. You can modify text, fill forms, draw signatures, blackout private details, and reorder pages without installing Adobe software or paying costly recurring fees.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>Yes, you do not need Adobe Acrobat or an Adobe Creative Cloud subscription to edit PDF files. Web-based editors like RealEditPDF provide a complete set of editing tools directly inside your web browser. You can modify text, fill forms, draw signatures, blackout private details, and reorder pages without installing Adobe software or paying costly recurring fees.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-can-i-edit-a-pdf-for-free-online",
    question: "Can I edit a PDF for free online?",
    category: "free",
    categoryLabel: "Online Editing",
    shortKeywords: "can i edit a pdf for free online website no registration instant",
    answerHtml: `<p>Yes, you can edit a PDF for free online at <a href="https://realeditpdf.com/" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF.com</a>. Simply visit the site on your computer or mobile device, drop your PDF into the editor, and begin editing immediately. There is no user registration, no email verification, and no software installation required. Your document remains securely inside your browser memory for total privacy.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>Yes, you can edit a PDF for free online at RealEditPDF.com. Simply visit the site on your computer or mobile device, drop your PDF into the editor, and begin editing immediately. There is no user registration, no email verification, and no software installation required. Your document remains securely inside your browser memory for total privacy.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-what-is-the-best-pdf-editor",
    question: "What is the best PDF editor?",
    category: "howto",
    categoryLabel: "Best Editor",
    shortKeywords: "what is the best pdf editor top rated private free webassembly smallpdf ilovepdf alternative",
    answerHtml: `<p>The best PDF editor for speed, security, and everyday use is <a href="#editor-anchor" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF</a>. Unlike cloud converters that store your private documents on external servers and enforce daily task caps, RealEditPDF runs 100% in-browser with zero file limits, complete data privacy, and instant WebAssembly rendering. For complex high-end commercial prepress, Adobe Acrobat Pro is traditional, but for free, effortless text editing, signing, and organizing, RealEditPDF is the top-rated browser choice.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>The best PDF editor for speed, security, and everyday use is RealEditPDF. Unlike cloud converters that store your private documents on external servers and enforce daily task caps, RealEditPDF runs 100% in-browser with zero file limits, complete data privacy, and instant WebAssembly rendering. For complex high-end commercial prepress, Adobe Acrobat Pro is traditional, but for free, effortless text editing, signing, and organizing, RealEditPDF is the top-rated browser choice.</p>"
  },
  {
    id: "faq-how-to-edit-a-pdf-online-on-a-phone",
    question: "How to edit a PDF online on a phone?",
    category: "devices",
    categoryLabel: "Mobile Guide",
    shortKeywords: "how to edit a pdf online on a phone iphone android touchscreen signature text",
    answerHtml: `<p>To edit a PDF online on a phone, launch your mobile browser (Safari on iPhone or Chrome on Android) and go to <a href="https://realeditpdf.com/" class="text-link font-semibold underline hover:text-ink">RealEditPDF.com</a>. Tap <strong>Select PDF Document</strong> to choose a file from your phone storage or cloud files. Use the touch-optimized toolbar to insert typography, mask and update text with whiteout, sign documents using your fingertip, or delete and rotate pages. Once done, tap <strong>Download PDF</strong> to save the modified document directly to your smartphone.</p>`,
    answerJsonLd: "<p>To edit a PDF online on a phone, launch your mobile browser (Safari on iPhone or Chrome on Android) and go to RealEditPDF.com. Tap Select PDF Document to choose a file from your phone storage or cloud files. Use the touch-optimized toolbar to insert typography, mask and update text with whiteout, sign documents using your fingertip, or delete and rotate pages. Once done, tap Download PDF to save the completed document directly to your phone's downloads.</p>"
  }
];

// Generate exact JSON-LD matching Schema.org FAQPage specification
const faqJsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "FAQPage",
  "mainEntity": faqs.map((faq) => ({
    "@type": "Question",
    "name": faq.question,
    "acceptedAnswer": {
      "@type": "Answer",
      "text": faq.answerJsonLd
    }
  }))
};
---

<section id="faq" class="py-12 sm:py-20 scroll-mt-20">
  <div class="glass-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 lg:p-10 border border-hairline bg-canvas-elevated/70 shadow-sm space-y-8">
    
    <!-- Section Header with Badges & Counter -->
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-end justify-between gap-4 border-b border-hairline pb-6">
      <div class="space-y-2 max-w-2xl">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas px-3 py-1 text-xs font-mono font-semibold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 uppercase tracking-wider shadow-whisper">
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8.228 9c.549-1.165 2.03-2 3.772-2 2.21 0 4 1.343 4 3 0 1.4-1.278 2.575-3.006 2.907-.542.104-.994.54-.994 1.093m0 3h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          <span>Frequently Asked Questions</span>
          <span class="text-hairline">•</span>
          <span class="text-mute">{faqs.length} Answers</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink">
          Frequently Asked Questions About PDF Editing
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm text-body leading-relaxed">
          Detailed answers to common questions about editing, signing, redacting, and managing PDF documents online for free.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Controls: Expand/Collapse All -->
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 self-start md:self-end">
        <button
          type="button"
          id="faq-expand-all-btn"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas hover:bg-canvas-elevated text-xs font-medium text-ink transition-colors shadow-whisper cursor-pointer"
        >
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
          </svg>
          <span>Expand All</span>
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          id="faq-collapse-all-btn"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-lg border border-hairline bg-canvas hover:bg-canvas-elevated text-xs font-medium text-mute hover:text-ink transition-colors shadow-whisper cursor-pointer"
        >
          <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M5 15l7-7 7 7" />
          </svg>
          <span>Collapse All</span>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Interactive Search and Filter Bar -->
    <div class="space-y-3">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-3 items-stretch sm:items-center justify-between">
        <!-- Live Search Input -->
        <div class="relative flex-1">
          <div class="absolute inset-y-0 left-0 pl-3.5 flex items-center pointer-events-none text-mute">
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M21 21l-6-6m2-5a7 7 0 11-14 0 7 7 0 0114 0z" />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="faq-search-input"
            placeholder="Search FAQs (e.g., mac, phone, free, text, adobe, sign)..."
            class="w-full pl-10 pr-9 py-2.5 rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas text-ink placeholder:text-mute text-sm focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-link/30 focus:border-link transition-all"
            aria-label="Search frequently asked questions"
          />
          <button
            type="button"
            id="faq-search-clear"
            class="absolute inset-y-0 right-0 pr-3 flex items-center text-mute hover:text-ink hidden cursor-pointer"
            aria-label="Clear search"
          >
            <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-4 w-4" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M6 18L18 6M6 6l12 12" />
            </svg>
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- Live FAQ Counter Indicator -->
        <div id="faq-match-count" class="text-xs font-mono text-mute px-1 self-center shrink-0">
          Showing <span id="faq-count-num" class="font-bold text-ink">{faqs.length}</span> of {faqs.length} questions
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Quick Category Chips -->
      <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1.5 pt-1" id="faq-category-pills">
        <button
          type="button"
          data-category="all"
          class="faq-filter-chip active rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium border border-link bg-link text-white shadow-whisper transition-all cursor-pointer"
        >
          All ({faqs.length})
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-category="free"
          class="faq-filter-chip rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium border border-hairline bg-canvas text-body hover:text-ink hover:bg-canvas-elevated transition-all cursor-pointer"
        >
          Free & Unlimited ({faqs.filter(f => f.category === 'free').length})
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-category="devices"
          class="faq-filter-chip rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium border border-hairline bg-canvas text-body hover:text-ink hover:bg-canvas-elevated transition-all cursor-pointer"
        >
          Mac & Mobile ({faqs.filter(f => f.category === 'devices').length})
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-category="howto"
          class="faq-filter-chip rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium border border-hairline bg-canvas text-body hover:text-ink hover:bg-canvas-elevated transition-all cursor-pointer"
        >
          How-To Guides ({faqs.filter(f => f.category === 'howto').length})
        </button>
        <button
          type="button"
          data-category="basics"
          class="faq-filter-chip rounded-full px-3 py-1 text-xs font-medium border border-hairline bg-canvas text-body hover:text-ink hover:bg-canvas-elevated transition-all cursor-pointer"
        >
          PDF Basics ({faqs.filter(f => f.category === 'basics').length})
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Accordion Items List -->
    <div id="faq-items-container" class="space-y-3">
      {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
        <details
          id={faq.id}
          data-category={faq.category}
          data-keywords={`${faq.question} ${faq.shortKeywords}`}
          class="faq-item group rounded-xl border border-hairline bg-canvas/70 p-4 transition-all duration-200 open:bg-canvas-elevated open:shadow-whisper open:border-link/30 hover:border-hairline-soft"
        >
          <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-3 text-left font-semibold text-ink text-[15px] sm:text-[16px] select-none">
            <div class="flex items-center gap-3 flex-1">
              <span class="inline-flex h-6 px-2 items-center justify-center rounded-md font-mono text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider bg-canvas border border-hairline text-link shrink-0">
                Q{index + 1}
              </span>
              <span class="capitalize-first leading-snug">
                {faq.question.endsWith('?') ? faq.question : `${faq.question}?`}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2 shrink-0 ml-2">
              <span class="hidden sm:inline-block font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-wider px-2 py-0.5 rounded-full border border-hairline bg-canvas text-mute">
                {faq.categoryLabel}
              </span>
              <span class="flex h-6 w-6 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-canvas border border-hairline text-mute group-open:rotate-180 group-open:text-link transition-transform duration-200">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
                  <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7" />
                </svg>
              </span>
            </div>
          </summary>
          <div class="mt-3 text-sm text-body leading-relaxed space-y-2 border-t border-hairline/60 pt-3 text-[14px] sm:text-[15px]">
            <Fragment set:html={faq.answerHtml} />
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}

      <!-- Zero search results fallback notice -->
      <div id="faq-no-results" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-dashed border-hairline p-8 text-center bg-canvas/40 space-y-2">
        <p class="text-base font-semibold text-ink">No matching questions found</p>
